/* The header for this test is at the BOTTOM of this file, below the script.
   It is there because a constant inside a leading comment can swallow the
   rest of the file in the engine - see RMSTEST_56 and the directory README.
   Nothing below the script can do any harm. */

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

<ELEVATION_GENERATION>


<CLIFF_GENERATION>
  min_number_of_cliffs 20
  max_number_of_cliffs 20
  min_length_of_cliff 2
  max_length_of_cliff 2
  cliff_curliness 10
  min_distance_cliffs 4

<TERRAIN_GENERATION>


<OBJECTS_GENERATION>

  /* Control. Proves the map generated at all, so that zero cliffs can be read
     as a cliff result rather than as a broken script. */
  create_object FORAGE
  {
    number_of_objects 25
    set_gaia_object_only
  }

<CONNECTION_GENERATION>

/*
RMSTEST_45a - arm 1 of 3. Minimum cliff length BELOW the documented floor.
Feeds: preview-design Sec.6.3, cliffs.ts, Sec.15 item 17(b)

READ RMSTEST_45b's HEADER FIRST. It carries the full question, the three
predictions and the reading rule for all three arms. This file is arm 1 and its
header is deliberately short so the three scripts stay byte-comparable.

THIS ARM: minimum 2, maximum 2. Both below the documented floor of 3.

WHY THREE FILES RATHER THAN THREE ARMS ON ONE MAP
The cliff section holds no block command. It is a bare list of standalone
attributes sitting directly in the section, and the last one written wins, so a
single map can only ever express ONE cliff configuration. Sec.15 item 17(b) asks
for "three arms on one map" and that is not constructible. Three scripts,
identical apart from the two length lines, is the same experiment.

GENERATE AT NORMAL (200), any player count. TWO RUNS.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --clusters
  Count cliff units. Two runs because the count is a distribution and only the
  zero-versus-nonzero distinction is binary.

BEFORE RUNNING ANY OF THE THREE, LOAD THE COMMUNITY MAP WHOSE NAME CLAIMS
CLIFFS AND WHOSE SCRIPT SETS A SUB-3 MINIMUM. It is either the counter-example
that kills the rule outright or the strongest confirmation available, and it
costs nothing.
*/
